// EXPECT: [E131]
// An `extern` may not declare a slice parameter. D-40, fixed 2026-09-16.
//
// A slice is a Lain value; C has no type for one. Whatever the declaration emitted it could not
// describe the callee: it was `const Slice_u8*` while the call site passed the decomposed data
// pointer, so even forwarding a `u8[]` parameter to such an extern warned. `extern` exists to
// describe functions Lain did not write, and a C function takes a pointer and, separately, a
// length — which is how `std/` already declares every one of its 143 externs.
//
// A SENTINEL slice (`u8[:0]`) is exempt: it is NUL-terminated, so it genuinely is a C string.

extern proc c_write(s u8[])

func main() i32 {
    return 0
}
